# Always ship to Vercel Production (`main`)

Isaac QAs on **Production** (`follow-the-crowd.vercel.app`). Vercel **branch Previews show "No target"** and are useless for device checks.

**Standing rule (locked 2026-08-06):** when a task is finished and the build is green, land it on **`main` in the same turn** so Production deploys. Do not leave completed work only on a `cursor/*` / feature Preview branch. Do not wait for a separate "push to Vercel" ask.

1. Commit and push the working branch.
2. Fast-forward or merge into **`main`** and push `origin/main`.
3. Mention in the summary that Production will pick it up (commit hash).

Large or risky work may open a PR first; once done, still merge to `main` the same turn unless Isaac said Preview-only.

Do not force-push `main`. Authoritative preference: `docs/handoff/USER-PREFERENCES.md` (Git) and `HOW-WE-WORK.md`.
